  "body": "```py\r\nself.clock.call_later(\r\n    30, self.clock.looping_call, run_timeout_handler, 5000\r\n)\r\n```\r\n\r\nChanging this to the following would avoid a bit of hassle when debugging (see below);\r\n\r\n```py\r\nself.clock.call_later(\r\n    30, self.clock.looping_call(run_timeout_handler, 5000).start\r\n)\r\n```\r\n\r\nBecause `DelayedCall` implicitly expects a normal function/method to be passed to `call_later`, the `__repr__` function errors on the following line;\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/twisted/twisted/blob/65f382f43dfe9bec9d25d99ce0cb05db115f5fac/src/twisted/internet/base.py#L241\r\n\r\n`L.extend((\" \", self.func.__qualname__, \"(\"))`\r\n\r\nFunctions have a `__qualname__`, but object instances doesnt.\r\n\r\nWhen `DelayedCall.debug` is true (when debugging the reactor), it calculates a `repr` of itself on init, this means that *all* `DelayedCall`s go past that above line, which means that any `DelayedCall`s waiting on `LoopingCall` will error out.",
